  "_comment": "Spots permanently excluded from the surf-spot database. Matched by exact name against the candidate/enriched records. Grouped by reason for reviewability. great_lakes: freshwater Great Lakes spots that were carrying ocean WFO tags and validated FAR at 402-550 km as domain misses, because the pipeline fetched an Atlantic grid and looked for them hundreds of km inland. NOAA DOES run NWPS for Great Lakes WFOs, so these could in principle be served by retagging, but the swell-window and raycast model assumes distant swell propagation while Great Lakes surf is short-fetch wind sea that dies within hours of the wind dropping. Serving them properly is a separate project, not a retag. Excluded rather than deleted so the decision is recorded and a future seed rebuild does not reintroduce them.",
